// ===========================================================================
// 11. THE WAVE DIRECTOR  (GDD §2.6 + §8)
// ===========================================================================
// budget(tier, wave) = 15 + 45*tier + 72*wave, wave in 0..2, tier the 0..5
// SHADE TIER INDEX.  Read at tier 1, that is 60 + 72*wave.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHY THE BASE IS 15 AND NOT THE GDD'S 60 — GAME_DESIGN §2.6 vs §8
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// GDD §2.6 writes `budget(tier, wave) = 60 + 45*tier + 18*wave`.  GDD §8, the
// spec for the first sixty seconds, writes "0:36-0:55 | Wave 1, tier 1,
// budget 60".  Those two statements are not compatible: the §2.6 formula
// evaluated at tier 1 is 105, not 60.  The two are reconciled by the only
// reading that satisfies both — §2.6's `tier` is 1-BASED (the first hold you
// ever play is "tier 1"), while the implementation's `tier` is the 0..5 shade
// tier INDEX that worldgen and the fog ladder use, where a lit lantern is 0.
// So the shipped formula is the GDD's own escalation re-indexed:
//
//      60 + 45*(tier - 1)  ==  15 + 45*tier          identical for all tier
//
// and §8's anchor falls out of it exactly: director_budget(1, 0) == 60.
// `tools/probe_director.hml` pins that 60 with a LITERAL assertion, not with a
// re-derivation from these three constants, because a relative assertion is
// exactly how this drifted in the first place.
//
// WHAT 105 COST.  105 points against tier 1's mean pool cost of 3.35 is ~31
// bodies in wave 1 alone, which saturates the 14-body alive cap and holds it
// saturated; the wave then cannot clear, and every §8 beat downstream of the
// clear — WAVE 1 CLEARED, the path of lit lanterns, Odo, the village — never
// arrives.  MEASURED before: wave 1 unclearable.  After: 60 points, ~18 bodies.
//
// RESIDUAL DOC GAP, stated rather than papered over: §8 illustrates its 60
// points as "~4 Husks and 6 Wisps", which is 4*6 + 6*2 = 36 points, not 60, and
// 10 bodies, not 18.  60 points is the number §8 states outright, so 60 is what
// is implemented.  Closing the remaining gap would mean raising the per-body
// spawn COSTS, which live in `sim/director.hml` / `sim/ai.hml` — not this file.
export let g_DIR_BUDGET_BASE: i32 = 15;
export let g_DIR_BUDGET_PER_TIER: i32 = 45;
// 18 -> 72.  See THE NIGHT HOLD, at g_DIR_SPAWN_CADENCE_S below: re-basing the
// tier-1 wave-1 budget from 105 to 60 removes 45 points from every wave of
// every hold, and the per-wave escalation is what puts them back where they
// belong — at the END of the hold, which is where escalation is supposed to
// live.  Tier 1 now reads 60 / 132 / 204 instead of 105 / 123 / 141.
export let g_DIR_BUDGET_PER_WAVE: i32 = 72;
export let g_DIR_ALIVE_CAP: i32 = 14;
export let g_DIR_ONSCREEN_CAP: i32 = 8;
export let g_DIR_SPAWN_MIN_M: f64 = 24.0;
export let g_DIR_SPAWN_MAX_M: f64 = 40.0;
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE NIGHT HOLD IS 2:40, NOT THE GDD'S 3:20.  RATIFIED, MEASURED, 2026-07-29.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// GDD §2.6 closes with "Hold duration ≈ 3:20 (3 waves + gaps)".  THAT NUMBER IS
// NOT REACHABLE FROM THE GDD'S OWN DIRECTOR PARAMETERS and never was:
//
//     tier-1 budget 369 pts / 3.35 mean pool cost = 110 bodies
//     110 bodies x 1.2 s cadence = 132 s + 2 x 8 s of wave gaps = 148 s FLOOR
//     measured against the reference player: 157.7 s   (target 200 s)
//
// The floor is the shortest a hold can be *if the player deletes every body the
// instant it arrives*, so 3:20 was never inside the reachable band at the
// director's own numbers.  This is the same class of internal inconsistency as
// the GDD's cumulative XP column (W4-7 found it; the gate confirmed it wrong).
//
// THE ONE-CONSTANT FIX WAS THE WRONG TRADE.  Cadence 1.56 s does land 201.1 s,
// exactly on the GDD's target — by RELEASING BODIES MORE SLOWLY.  Measured, it
// drops peak-alive to 12 of the 14-body cap, so the cap never binds and the
// density the cap exists to bound is never reached.  Longer AND thinner.  A
// night hold whose crowding limit is never touched is not a night hold.
//
// THE DECISION (the owner's): KEEP THE DENSITY, ACCEPT ~2:40.
// Retuned as one pass over cadence + budget together, tier 1, 12 holds per
// point, against probe_director's reference player (whose only free parameter,
// `acq`, is the seconds of per-body engagement overhead — see that file):
//
//                       cadence  budget(1,·)   bodies  hold @acq 0.35   peak alive
//   before               1.20 s  105/123/141      110      157.7 s        8 @acq 1.2
//   rejected (thinner)   1.56 s  105/123/141      110      201.1 s       12 (cap never binds)
//   SHIPPED              1.15 s   60/132/204      118      162.3 s       13 @acq 1.2, 14 @1.6
//
// So the shipped hold is 2:42 at the reference player, 4 % denser in raw spawn
// rate than before, and MUCH denser late: peak-alive at a 1.2 s engagement
// overhead goes 8 -> 13 of 14, because the escalated wave 3 (204 pts, ~61
// bodies back to back) is where the crowd now happens.  The alive cap still
// binds hard from acq 1.6 s upward, in 12 of 12 holds.
//
// THE CEILING NOBODY WROTE DOWN: NIGHT IS 300 s (g_PHASE_DUSK_END -> 1.0 of a
// 960 s day).  `director_step` ABORTS a live hold at dawn, so total bodies are
// bounded by what the slowest survivable player can clear inside 300 s, not by
// taste.  MEASURED at 118 bodies: acq 2.0 s finishes at 273.9 s mean / 287.0 s
// worst — inside 300.  At 125 bodies (cadence 1.05 s, per-wave 80) holds began
// being aborted by dawn.  118 IS NEAR THAT CEILING.  If you raise the budget
// again, re-measure the acq 2.0 s column before you believe it.
//
// COSTS WERE NOT TOUCHED and could not be from here: the six per-body spawn
// costs live in `sim/director.hml` (mirrored by `ai_cost_of` in `sim/ai.hml`),
// neither of which this task owns.  They are the remaining lever, and the one
// that would close §8's "~4 Husks and 6 Wisps" body count as well.
export let g_DIR_SPAWN_CADENCE_S: f64 = 1.15;
export let g_DIR_WAVE_GAP_S: f64 = 8.0;
export let g_DIR_WAVES_PER_HOLD: i32 = 3;
export let g_DIR_SPAWN_BEHIND_BIAS: f64 = 0.70;      // fraction spawned behind view

// ===========================================================================
